Here is the commit message:
CLEANUP: hlua: fix CertCache class comment

CLASS_CERTCACHE is used to declare CertCache global object, not Regex one

This copy-paste typo introduced was in 30fcca18 ("MINOR: ssl/lua:
CertCache.set() allows to update an SSL certificate file")

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a copy-paste error in the comment associated with the `lua_setglobal(L, CLASS_CERTCACHE);` line, which incorrectly referred to the global object as "Regex" instead of the correct "CertCache." This mislabeling could lead to confusion for developers reading the code, as it does not accurately describe the functionality of the `CLASS_CERTCACHE` declaration.

